===Etymology===
From Italian [[scherzo#Italian|scherzo]].

===Pronunciation===
[[IPA]]: /'skɛ:tsəʊ/

===Noun===
{{en-noun2|'''scherzo'''|'''[[scherzos]]''' or '''[[scherzi]]'''}}

# {{music}} A piece of music or a [[movement]] from a larger piece such as a [[symphony]]; especially, a piece of music played in a playful manner.
#:*'''1980''': At seven Val knocked – three shorts and one long, out of the '''scherzo''' of Beethoven’s Fifth – and I rushed to open. — Anthony Burgess, ''Earthly Powers''

